Found under k16 (pre-existing, unchanged by it). Building a dist without a remote gives META.json "resources":{"bugtracker":{},"repository":{}}: the SUPPORT template stash of GenerateSection reads distmeta->{resources}{bugtracker}{web} and autovivifies the hashes. Check whether it is the weaver stash or another reader, and whether CPAN::Meta validation or metacpan care; leave the GitHub case byte-identical.

2026-11-09 20:45 Cause confirmed: hooking Pod::Weaver weave_document and diffing distmeta->{resources} after every step, only @GETTY/Support changes it (absent -> {bugtracker=>{}, repository=>{}}): the template stash of GenerateSection (lines 154-170) reads $input->{distmeta}{resources}{repository}{web} etc. and autovivifies in the dist own distmeta, the one META.json is written from. Fix (branch k22-k25, uncommitted yet): the around weave_section in Pod::Weaver::Section::Author::GETTY::Support passes GenerateSection a copy of distmeta with its own copy of resources; one level is enough (reading {x}{web} only creates x). Verified: no remote -> META without a resources key (main: {"bugtracker":{},"repository":{}}); github origin byte-identical. The old output was valid (CPAN::Meta validator accepts both), only noise.

2026-11-09 21:23 Tests (uncommitted): t/weaver_support.t +16: six distmeta inputs (no resources, empty, without bugtracker, empty bugtracker, bugtracker, bugtracker+repository+IRC); the caller's distmeta is deep-equal after the weave and $input->{distmeta} is the same reference; SUPPORT text unchanged; a weave without distmeta works and yields no section. t/support_build.t: full build without remote -> no resources key in distmeta and META.json, no empty bugtracker/repository. Counter-check against main: 5 of 6 weave cases and the no-remote build red (the bugtracker+repository case vivifies nothing on main either).

